Element-level B-bar (mean dilatation) for near-incompressible phases.

Opt-in via CCX_BBAR_NU: the Poisson ratio at or above which the volumetric
term is assembled from the ELEMENT-MEAN divergence operator instead of the
pointwise one. Unset, the behaviour is bit-for-bit the stock behaviour
(verified: identical to every printed digit on a homogeneous cube).

VERIFIED CORRECT, AND LARGELY USELESS HERE. Read both parts.

Correct: on a homogeneous cube with B-bar forced on for every element, E_eff
comes back 9.42999998e9 against an exact 9.43e9. Uniform strain has mean
divergence equal to its pointwise value, so B-bar must be a no-op there, and
it is.

Useless for linear tets: C3D4 has ONE integration point, so the element mean
of the divergence IS the pointwise value and B-bar is mathematically the
identity. Measured: E_x on an undrained layered cell is bit-identical with and
without it. This is not an implementation gap -- it is what the method is. The
+2.1 point volumetric excess measured at order 1 in
calculix/README.md CANNOT be recovered this way. Saving linear tets needs a
NODAL-AVERAGED B-bar, which averages volumetric strain over the patch of
elements sharing each node; that couples DOFs across elements, changes the
stiffness sparsity pattern, and therefore cannot live in e_c3d.f at all --
it needs mastruct.c and a new assembly path.

Acts only at order 2 (C3D10, 4 integration points), where it moves E_x on the
confined undrained layered cell by -11.5%.

KNOWN INCONSISTENCY. Only the stiffness is patched. resultsmech.f still
recovers internal forces with the standard B, so reaction forces are
inconsistent with the B-bar kinematics: the equilibrium cross-check
(volume-averaged stress against the reference-point reaction) reads ~1.0
instead of ~1e-7 whenever B-bar is active. Volume-averaged stress -- what the
homogenisation actually reads -- stays consistent, because the element mean of
lambda*div(u) is exactly the B-bar pressure. But the best available
verification is lost while this is on, which is why it is off by default.
Making it consistent means patching the internal-force recovery too.

    cd <ccx_2.23>
    git apply -p0 0002-bbar-mean-dilatation.patch
    cd src && make -j8

